To compile the server on Linux / macOS:
cc server.c adapter_svc.c utils.c -o server

To compile the server on Windows:
gcc server.c adapter_svc.c utils.c -o server.exe -lws2_32

To run (listens on port 8888):
./server

Data is stored in "people.dat" in the directory the server is run from
(it is created automatically).

Files:
  server.c        save_person / retrieve_person procedures
                  (no networking code; they store and read the file)
  adapter_svc.c   Server-side adapter (skeleton) and main()
  utils.c         Sockets: initialization, connection, close_socket
  server.h        Types, constants and prototypes
